WEBVTT

00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:10.334
Jackpot, baby! Whoo-hoo!

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:13.379
Well, I say we call it a night there, fellas.

00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:16.006
Hey, put the cash in my car, will you, Derek?

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.216
(LAUGHS)

00:00:18.092 --> 00:00:20.845
Well, you're one great card player, Mike.

00:00:21.178 --> 00:00:22.680
-Not so bad yourself.
-(GIGGLES)

00:00:23.681 --> 00:00:26.600
Except, I still can't tell how you cheated.

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.602
Cheated? Cheated?

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:30.855
Oh, I am offended.

00:00:30.938 --> 00:00:32.773
Come on, baby, let's cut some rug.

00:00:35.442 --> 00:00:37.945
Oh! What the...

00:00:38.028 --> 00:00:39.029
Oh. (CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:40.406
How did that get there?

00:00:41.073 --> 00:00:43.033
-Run for it, baby!
-Hey!

00:00:45.202 --> 00:00:46.287
BOSS BEAR: Get him!

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.627
(SCREAMS)

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:56.130
Excuse me!

00:00:57.631 --> 00:00:59.550
BOSS BEAR: Don't let him get away!

00:01:01.385 --> 00:01:02.595
(GRUNTING)

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:07.766
-Thanks, Derek!
-BOSS BEAR: Out of the way!

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.310
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:18.777
So long, suckers! (LAUGHS)

00:01:22.531 --> 00:01:23.991
(GROWLING)

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.161
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

00:01:28.913 --> 00:01:30.122
Good morning, Buster.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.415
Hey, Eddie, how are you?

00:01:31.498 --> 00:01:32.833
Good. How's the show going?

00:01:32.917 --> 00:01:34.251
Ah, it's going great.

00:01:34.335 --> 00:01:36.420
And, hey,
that's a sharp jacket you've got on today.

00:01:36.503 --> 00:01:38.172
Oh, thanks.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.298
Wait.

00:01:40.341 --> 00:01:41.842
(SHRIEKS) What are you doing here?

00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:45.095
Eddie, you can't come visit your nana
without bringing her some flowers.

00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:46.180
Here.

00:01:46.263 --> 00:01:48.724
-What? No! Buster, no! Don't go in there!
-(RINGS DOORBELL)

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:50.768
-Yes, can I help...
-Buster!

00:01:50.935 --> 00:01:52.937
Ah, Nana!

00:01:57.107 --> 00:01:59.693
Just look at you, dear. Wow!

00:01:59.777 --> 00:02:01.654
You don't look a day over 90!

00:02:01.737 --> 00:02:02.863
Oh, my gosh!

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.573
Buster Moon!

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.408
We met at Eddie's graduation.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:07.743
Oh, lucky me.

00:02:07.826 --> 00:02:09.912
A visit from my useless grandson

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:12.456
and his ghastly little theater friend.

00:02:12.539 --> 00:02:14.208
Look at that, she remembers me.

00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:15.334
Okay, Nana,

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:19.254
how would you like to be
the sponsor for a very prestigious prize?

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:22.216
Not for that singing contest
I saw on the news.

00:02:22.299 --> 00:02:23.384
That's the one!

00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:25.594
Oh, I see.

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:28.055
You don't have the money, do you?

00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:29.932
Well, we don't quite have it all locked in...

00:02:30.099 --> 00:02:31.850
Well, you'll not get a cent out of me.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:32.893
Nana, please just listen to me...

00:02:32.977 --> 00:02:34.019
No, absolutely not.

00:02:34.103 --> 00:02:35.187
Don't listen to him, Nana.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:36.855
I'm not listening to either of you.

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:39.817
Lapsang souchong. No sugar.
And be quick about it.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.026
Uh, Nana...

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:43.153
I don't know how to make tea.

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:46.198
(OPERA MUSIC PLAYING)

00:02:46.323 --> 00:02:48.325
Wow. I saw this show when I was a kid.

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:50.577
Nana, you were absolutely amazing.

00:02:50.744 --> 00:02:53.330
Please, this flattery is futile.

00:02:53.414 --> 00:02:56.291
I have no intention
of bailing you out. (GIGGLES)

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:57.918
Your pathetic shows are the reason

00:02:58.002 --> 00:02:59.962
that theater no longer has an audience.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:03.173
Oh, but this show is gonna
pack them in like it did in the good old days.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.385
They were not good old days, Mr. Moon.

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:09.263
They were magnificent.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.348
And that theater of yours,

00:03:11.515 --> 00:03:15.227
it was a palace of wonder and magic.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:16.687
But, Nana, it still is.

00:03:16.854 --> 00:03:18.397
EDDIE: Yeah, right. Ow!

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.109
I can recall the ushers in their velvet suits.

00:03:22.443 --> 00:03:25.612
Queues a mile long just to get a ticket.

00:03:25.696 --> 00:03:30.367
The curtain rising over that glorious stage.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:34.121
Music and light bringing dreams to life?

00:03:34.288 --> 00:03:35.581
Precisely.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.875
Well, it's just like you remember it.

00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:40.878
In fact, I've made it even more spectacular.

00:03:40.961 --> 00:03:42.171
-EDDIE: No, you haven't.
-Shh.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:45.299
Come see for yourself.
A special performance just for you.

00:03:45.382 --> 00:03:46.508
What do you say, Nana?

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.887
I say, you are a liar, Mr. Moon.

00:03:50.554 --> 00:03:51.722
EDDIE: Okay, well...

00:03:51.805 --> 00:03:53.182
We're done now. Thank you, Nana.

00:03:53.307 --> 00:03:55.642
But anything's better than
spending another evening

00:03:55.726 --> 00:03:57.519
playing checkers with this old fart.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:58.645
What?

00:03:58.729 --> 00:04:01.065
Great! It's gonna blow you away, Nana.

00:04:01.148 --> 00:04:02.858
And that is no lie!

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:04.777
Now, listen up!

00:04:05.027 --> 00:04:07.446
Tomorrow we're going to have
a full preview of the show.

00:04:07.529 --> 00:04:10.908
And our audience will be none
other than Miss Nana Noodleman.

00:04:10.991 --> 00:04:13.410
Nana Noodleman? She's still alive?

00:04:13.869 --> 00:04:15.662
Oh, yes, and believe me,

00:04:15.746 --> 00:04:17.873
she's got some
pretty high standards, all right.

00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:20.209
So, today we're gonna have
a full dress rehearsal.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:22.503
And I want to see you
light up the stage, folks!

00:04:22.586 --> 00:04:23.545
Well, that's cool.

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:24.630
Meena, Miss Crawly...

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.092
-What do you think?
-MISS CRAWLY: Wow, it's so ambitious.

00:04:28.175 --> 00:04:29.343
Yeah, are you sure about this?

00:04:29.426 --> 00:04:31.720
I promised Nana something spectacular.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.222
And this... (CHUCKLES)

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:35.015
-It's gonna blow her away.
-Oh, yes.

00:04:35.099 --> 00:04:36.350
Two minutes, everybody.

00:04:37.059 --> 00:04:38.143
BIG DADDY: (OVER RADIO) Johnny?

00:04:38.519 --> 00:04:40.062
Johnny, where are you?

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.274
Johnny? Answer the walkie-talkie.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.485
(STAMMERS) Yeah, Dad.
I'm here. I'm here. What's wrong?

00:04:46.568 --> 00:04:48.737
We got the call. Shipment's coming in.

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.405
-Tonight?
-Not tonight.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:51.782
Now.

00:04:51.865 --> 00:04:54.409
Meet us on the corner
of Hector Street in two minutes.

00:04:57.538 --> 00:04:58.539
(LAUGHING)

00:05:00.374 --> 00:05:01.458
(TIRES SCREECH)

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:09.174
Stay here. We'll be back in exactly 37...

00:05:09.258 --> 00:05:11.885
Yeah, 37 minutes.
Yep. You've told me repeatedly.

00:05:18.976 --> 00:05:20.060
I can make it.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:28.110
Bravo, Mike. Nana is gonna love that!

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:30.571
Aw, you're too kind, Mr. Moon.

00:05:30.654 --> 00:05:32.698
BUSTER: And I myself
am loving the new suit, sir.

00:05:32.781 --> 00:05:35.033
Okay, can we see Ash next, please?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.744
Ash, let's get you out here!

00:05:38.662 --> 00:05:41.373
Oh! Stand back.
Moody teenager coming through.

00:05:41.456 --> 00:05:42.499
MEENA: Good luck, Ash.

00:05:42.916 --> 00:05:44.126
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:52.676
(SINGING WEAKLY)

00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:04.021
(VOICE BREAKING)

00:06:07.482 --> 00:06:09.318
(SOBBING)

00:06:15.282 --> 00:06:16.325
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:18.994
Okay. Enough of that! Cut it! Cut it!

00:06:19.077 --> 00:06:19.786
(MUSIC STOPS)

00:06:19.953 --> 00:06:20.704
(ASH CRYING)

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:22.372
I don't think anyone's gonna
call her after that.

00:06:22.456 --> 00:06:23.749
Okay, Ash. Um...

00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:25.959
Hey, come on, Ash.

00:06:27.377 --> 00:06:29.087
What is it? Do you not like the dress?

00:06:29.296 --> 00:06:30.297
(CONTINUES CRYING)

00:06:30.964 --> 00:06:33.467
Ow! Ow!

00:06:33.675 --> 00:06:34.885
Ash, what's wrong?

